{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790263362327,"sessionID":"ses_f2bff1df3ffem83Fc7tRT81gko","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_5c556eca0be549cdac6a93e4","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Explore project structure","prompt":"Explore the /workspace directory thoroughly. I need to understand:\n1. The overall project structure (files, directories)\n2. Find the shader file at res://shaders/weapon_clip_and_fov_shader.gdshader\n3. Find any files related to view model, weapon view model, MeshInstance3D references\n4. Find any GDScript files that reference weapon view model nodes\n5. Look for any existing material/shader swap logic\n\nReturn:\n- The full directory tree\n- The contents of the shader file\n- Key files related to weapon view model and any material/shader handling\n- Any existing patterns for replacing materials with shader materials","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"<task id=\"ses_f2bfed465ffe3a4TwUnZnPtqTL\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nHere is a complete and thorough analysis of the `/workspace` directory.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Full Directory Tree\n\n```\n/workspace/\n├── project.godot\n├── task_config.json\n├── .godot/\n│   ├── .gdignore\n│   ├── uid_cache.bin\n│   ├── scene_groups_cache.cfg\n│   ├── global_script_class_cache.cfg\n│   └── editor/\n│       ├── filesystem_cache10\n│       ├── main.tscn-folding-3ad5c15c4f3250da0cc7c1af1770d85f.cfg\n│       └── project_metadata.cfg\n├── scenes/\n│   └── main.tscn\n├── scripts/\n│   ├── weapon_manager.gd\n│   └── weapon_manager.gd.uid\n└── shaders/\n    ├── weapon_clip_and_fov_shader.gdshader\n    └── weapon_clip_and_fov_shader.gdshader.uid\n```\n\n### Key source files (non-engine/non-hidden)\n| File | Path |\n|------|------|\n| Project config | `/workspace/project.godot` |\n| Task instructions | `/workspace/task_config.json` |\n| Main scene | `/workspace/scenes/main.tscn` |\n| Weapon manager script | `/workspace/scripts/weapon_manager.gd` |\n| FOV/clip shader | `/workspace/shaders/weapon_clip_and_fov_shader.gdshader` |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Shader File Contents\n\n**File:** `/workspace/shaders/weapon_clip_and_fov_shader.gdshader` (57 lines)\n\nThis is a `spatial` (3D) shader, auto-converted from a `StandardMaterial3D`. It has:\n\n- **Standard PBR uniforms:** `albedo`, `texture_albedo`, `roughness`, `texture_metallic`, `texture_roughness`, `specular`, `metallic`, `texture_normal`, `normal_scale`, plus UV scale/offset uniforms.\n- **Custom uniform:** `viewmodel_fov` (default `75.0`).\n- **Vertex shader logic:** When `viewmodel_fov > 0.0`, it modifies the projection matrix to change the FOV, and then mixes `POSITION.z` toward `POSITION.w` by a factor of `0.9` to push the weapon model's depth close to the near clip plane -- solving the \"weapon clipping through walls\" problem.\n- **Fragment shader:** Standard PBR texture sampling and output (ALBEDO, METALLIC, ROUGHNESS, SPECULAR, NORMAL_MAP).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Files Related to View Model / Weapon View Model / MeshInstance3D\n\n### Scene tree from `main.tscn` -- the view model hierarchy:\n\n```\nMain (Node3D)\n└── WeaponManager (Node3D, script: weapon_manager.gd)\n    └── ViewModel (Node3D)\n        └── Knife (MeshInstance3D)\n```\n\nThe `\"Knife\"` node is a `MeshInstance3D` with a `BoxMesh` (placeholder weapon mesh). It has an inline `StandardMaterial3D` with albedo `(0.2, 0.7, 0.9)`, metallic `0.2`, roughness `0.8`.\n\n### Script referencing the view model:\n\n**File:** `/workspace/scripts/weapon_manager.gd` -- this is the **only GDScript file** in the entire project. It references the view model on line 3:\n\n```gdscript\n@onready var view_model_container: Node3D = $ViewModel\n```\n\nAnd it has a **stub function** on line 8 that is clearly meant to be implemented:\n\n```gdscript\nfunc apply_clip_and_fov_shader_to_view_model(node3d: Node3D, fov_or_negative_for_unchanged := -1.0) -> void:\n    pass\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. GDScript Files Referencing Weapon View Model Nodes\n\nThere is only **one GDScript file** in the project: `/workspace/scripts/weapon_manager.gd`. It references:\n\n| Line | Reference | Purpose |\n|------|-----------|---------|\n| 3 | `@onready var view_model_container: Node3D = $ViewModel` | Grabs the ViewModel node from the scene tree |\n| 8 | `func apply_clip_and_fov_shader_to_view_model(...)` | Stub function to be filled with shader swap logic |\n\nNo other `.gd` files exist anywhere in the project.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Existing Material/Shader Swap Logic\n\n**There is no existing material/shader swap logic implemented.** The relevant function is a completely empty stub:\n\n```gdscript\nfunc apply_clip_and_fov_shader_to_view_model(node3d: Node3D, fov_or_negative_for_unchanged := -1.0) -> void:\n    pass\n```\n\nThere are also **zero** `.tres` resource files and **zero** references to `material_override`, `surface_material`, `ShaderMaterial`, or `shader_material` anywhere in the codebase. No existing patterns for material swapping exist yet.\n\n---\n\n## Summary of Task Context (from `task_config.json`)\n\nThe task at hand is explicitly stated:\n\n> Implement the view model clip shader swap on the weapon view model node. Add logic that finds MeshInstance3D nodes under the view model, replaces each surface material with a ShaderMaterial that uses `res://shaders/weapon_clip_and_fov_shader.gdshader`, copies the base material albedo/metallic/roughness parameters into the shader, and sets the `viewmodel_fov` shader parameter to 54.0 when applying the shader.\n\n### What needs to be built (all in `weapon_manager.gd`):\n\n1. Recursively find all `MeshInstance3D` children under the `ViewModel` node.\n2. For each mesh, iterate over surface material slots.\n3. For each `BaseMaterial3D` (StandardMaterial3D, ORMMaterial3D, etc.), create a new `ShaderMaterial` using `res://shaders/weapon_clip_and_fov_shader.gdshader`.\n4. Copy the base material's `albedo_color`, `metallic`, `roughness` into the shader's uniforms (`albedo`, `metallic`, `roughness`).\n5. Set `viewmodel_fov` to `54.0` on the shader material.\n6. Replace the surface material with the new `ShaderMaterial`.\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_f2bff1df3ffem83Fc7tRT81gko","sessionId":"ses_f2bfed465ffe3a4TwUnZnPtqTL","model":{"modelID":"deepseek-v4-pro","providerID":"openai"},"truncated":false},"title":"Explore project structure","time":{"start":1790263241632,"end":1790263362316}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_b01e3c75-cfb0-4907-8fdc-567596fe1495"}},"id":"prt_0d4012b8e0015ODWhX6WnU7NvW","sessionID":"ses_f2bff1df3ffem83Fc7tRT81gko","messageID":"msg_0d400e3b9001m21h6YH2nfxB1l"}}
